        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomingdale%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The New Jersey Midland Railroad ran tracks through the area, placing a Bloomingdale station in what today is Riverdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomingdale%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bloomingdale Cornet Band has performed continuously since 1884, while Donald School, built in 1886, remains a historic landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomingdale%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dutch farmers settled the area in the mid‑1700s, moving west from Pompton Plains to farm the fertile valley that would become Bloomingdale.",
